thletes/15510"} "Silvio Martinello"] ". He took the lead early in the final and won the gold medal relatively easily. Six riders remained together on the final lap, with Canada’s " [:a {:href "/athletes/17123"} "Brian Walton"] " winning the final sprint to move up to a silver medal. The bronze medal went to Australia’s " [:a {:href "/athletes/15926"} "Stuart O’Grady"] ". O’Grady had a cardiac condition, supraventricular tachycardia (SVT), and the day before the points race had suffered a seizure, but recovered to race despite that. Martinello would also win the 1997 World Championships."] "\n"] [:table {:class "table table-striped"} [:thead {} [:tr {} [:th {} "Pos"] [:th {} "Competitor"] [:th {} "NOC"] [:th {} "Lap Margin"] [:th {} "Points"] [:th {}] [:th {}] [:th {}]]] [:tbody {} [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {} "1"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/athletes/15510"} "Silvio Martinello"]] [:td {} [:a {:href "/countries/ITA"} [:img {:style "padding-right: 2px; vertical-align: middle", :src "https://olympedia-flags.s3.eu-central-1.amazonaws.com/ITA.png"}] "ITA"]] [:td {} "---"] [:td {} "37"] [:td {} [:span {:class "Gold"} "Gold"]] [:td {}] [:td {}]] [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {} "2"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/athletes/17123"} "Brian Walton"]] [:td {} [:a {:href "/countries/CAN"} [:img {:style "padding-right: 2px; vertical-align: middle", :src "https://olympedia-flags.s3.eu-central-1.amazonaws.com/CAN.png"}] "CAN"]] [:td {} "same lap"] [:td {} "29"] [:td {} [:span {:class "Silver"} "Silver"]] [:td {}] [:td {}]] [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {} "3"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/athletes/15926"} "Stuart O'Grady"]] [:td {} [:a {:href "/countries/AUS"} [:img {:style "padding-right: 2px; vertical-align: middle", :src "https://olympedia-flags.s3.eu-central-1.amazonaws.com/AUS.png"}] "AUS"]] [:td {} "same lap"] [:td {} "25"] [:td {} [:span {:class "Bronze"} "Bronze"]] [:td {}] [:td {}]] [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {} "4"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/athletes/14877"} "Vasyl Yakovlev"]] [:td 